    {
      "id": 47034,
      "name": "Matchstickman",
      "username": "Matchstickman",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/matchstickman/{size}/1880_2.png",
      "created_at": "2012-11-29T10:45:20.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I think the prescedent would be cards that target multiple things, e.g. hoarfire, it damages two separate targets but they can still be the same named card, just not the same physical card (e.g. 2 copies of gene-bound ion-lancer when facing Voss), they are considered different targets, not the same one twice.</p>",
      "post_number": 8,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:20:32.095Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
